      "reference": "Diablo II, Baldur's Gate, Darkest Dungeon dungeons",
      "goals": [
        "every room and zone connected: a clear route from the entrance to the deepest room (the boss), with side rooms and a loop or two",
        "rooms of varied shape and size by purpose (crypt halls, narrow corridors, a large boss chamber), never a grid of equal boxes",
        "thick, continuous walls with doors set in them; solid rock outside the rooms",
        "immersive lighting: dark overall, warm pools of light from torches on walls and braziers, falling off into shadow",
        "props against walls and in corners (sarcophagi in rows, debris in corners, chests in dead ends), a strong focal piece per room (an altar, a throne), the middle of rooms kept walkable",
        "floors varied: cracked stone, rubble, puddles, a few stains, never one tile repeated",
        "items with a story: a key lies on the near side of its locked door, in a room found before it (never behind it, rarely right beside it), a lever by its gate, traps in corridors, bones near the lair"
      ]
    }
  },
